Description: Use full .js specifiers in relative imports
 es-html-parser is compiled to CommonJS, where extensionless imports such as
 "../constants" resolve. This package ships native ES modules, where Node
 requires the full specifier, so every relative import names its .js file or
 its directory's index.js, and type-only re-exports use "export type" as
 isolatedModules requires. TypeScript maps each .js specifier to its .ts
 source at compile time.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Test: npm run typecheck; npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-10-14
